<title>UK: UK notes in circulation rise 7.4 pct in week.</title>
<headline>UK notes in circulation rise 7.4 pct in week.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-10-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>British bank notes in circulation rose 7.4 percent in the week to October 31 over the equivalent week a year ago, figures from the Bank of England showed.</p>
<p>Last week the rise was also 7.4 percent.</p>
<p>(figures in rounded billions of stg) -</p>
<p>			   Latest week  Previous week  Year-ago week</p>
<p> Notes in circulation  20.78	  20.72	     19.36</p>
<p> Bankers deposits	2.23	   2.02		1.71</p>
<p>-- Mike Peacock, London Newsroom +44 171 542 5109</p>
</text>
